6171523}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "647f22db-be6c-5030-ad2b-0f6c51d539bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-98033" :question/problem "Which of the following regions is *not* connected?" :question/worked-solution "A region $D$ is connected if every pair of points in $D$ can be joined by a smooth curve or a path in $D.$ \n\nAmong the given options, the only one that does not satisfy this definition is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/72f59260e2d8e20a163fb4462a6332c4fafd00078a6e851806b30b9c005a0ae3.png)\n\nNote that if we take two points $P$ and $Q$, as shown below, there is no path lying entirely within the region that connects them.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/72aac3f5d5f3b58e571df5c2b8d35523af379dabf66b40c3018eba573b119fca.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172594 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1af47ea-6253-5d58-9b94-31e52de27106" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Simply-Connected Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a72f5cd1-f995-5bf9-9c2f-b15b07664c0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/q-98035-a-2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171530} {:answer/id #uuid "bb6440c1-9147-5ac2-9a38-c145bc5403e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/q-98035-a-3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171531} {:answer/id #uuid "fabfa234-8bf2-53a6-89ea-9f9e8e769fbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/q-98035-a-4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171532} {:answer/id #uuid "3563f91c-c127-52a6-bc25-2af4533166cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/q-98035-a-5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171533} {:answer/id #uuid "451b0efb-73f1-58d5-84ba-01690e2c1afe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/q-98035-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "451b0efb-73f1-58d5-84ba-01690e2c1afe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/q-98035-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171534} :answer-field/id #uuid "780b37f2-853f-5e38-ae71-8da9c83932bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171529}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2eb47630-481d-5fa5-a91b-a7743799b27f" :question/math-academy-id "q-98035" :question/problem "Which of the following is *not* a simply connected region?" :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nAmong the given options, the only one that does not satisfy this definition is the following:\n\n \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/9a001b71c984559199c1457115621dbd111c69da50f741332b2396ce832ede08.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172595 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1af47ea-6253-5d58-9b94-31e52de27106" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Simply-Connected Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "991d14d6-f584-54a3-99eb-29960c372ebd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171536} {:answer/id #uuid "a5af7421-68de-547b-86a4-93017f0a1c4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171537} {:answer/id #uuid "b5b779fa-4c5d-5726-8990-3cda152f49b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171538} {:answer/id #uuid "f0fc5c92-477a-5cd6-a540-14d2eca13f58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171539} {:answer/id #uuid "1eaaf3ea-1b6a-52bf-bb97-41ecec4b5bfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1eaaf3ea-1b6a-52bf-bb97-41ecec4b5bfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171540} :answer-field/id #uuid "bebc62e1-5482-5ce4-89dd-f0906e6fc264" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171535}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "72da8c2e-5747-5cf0-addd-5e327ef519dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-98036" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/0045eda99f40f774d2ef21214522eebb0c53bffee304ba503a9076a7491cc648.png)\n\nWhich of the regions shown above are simply connected?" :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the regions: \n\n- Region I is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region II is not simply connected. Instead, this is a connected region that contains two holes.\n\n- Region III is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region IV is not simply connected. Instead, this is a region that consists of two pieces (it's not connected).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186372510 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d15f8fa8-f265-50da-b172-3ccb90895448" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connected Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dfe32fb-a9b3-5932-a800-439592d4478f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/ba346990bd792f1e4a9aed0d900ca087315544715a35cd5cd90049c99fdb84ba.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186372512} {:answer/id #uuid "d8ccb63c-1e8b-5440-9643-a4b2f7a78f5e" :answer/type {:db/ide