loses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the regions:  \n\n- Region I is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region II is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region III is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region IV is not simply connected. Instead, this is a connected region that contains a hole.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\""}]}
